Below is a lightweight Helm structure to create a dedicated Kubernetes namespace, install all services of the LoveAgain application, and expose them with basic monitoring and logging best‑practice components.

###1. Chart Overview- **Namespace** – `cue-platform` (namespace created by `templates/namespace.yaml`)- **Deployments** – One deployment per micro‑service (`AuthService`, `ProfileService`, `BookingService`, `PaymentService`, `ChatService`, `NotificationService`, `ReviewService`, ` SupportService`)- **Service** – Headless `ClusterIP` service for inter‑service communication + external `Ingress` for public API.- **Secrets** – Application secret keys are handled via `Secret` objects.- **Monitoring** – Simple Prometheus annotations for metrics collection; logs forwarded via sidecar (Fluent Bit).- **Helm Values** – You can change the image registry, tag, replicas, resource limits etc. in `values.yaml`.###2. Helm Chart Files####`helm-chart/Chart.yaml`
```yamlapiVersion: v2
name: cuedescription: A Helm chart for the Cue platform (microservices-based experience companion)
type: application
version: 0.1.0appVersion: "1.0.0"
```

####`helm-chart/values.yaml`
```yaml# Default values for cueimage:
 registry: ghcr.io/myorg tag: latestserviceAccount: falsenamespaces:
 create: true name: cue-platformreplicaCount:1resources:
 requests:
 cpu:200m memory:256Mi limits:
 cpu:500m memory:512MisecurityContext:
 runAsUser:1000 runAsGroup:1000# Service port mappingports:
 http:80 https:443# Monitoring/Loggingmonitoring:
 enabled: true prometheus:
 enabled: true fluentbit:
 enabled: true# Per‑service overridesauthService:
 replicas:1 memory:512Mi env:
 - name: ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT value: ProductionpaymentService:
 replicas:1```

####`helm-chart/templates/namespace.yaml`
```yaml{{- if .Values.namespaces.create }}
apiVersion: v1kind: Namespacemetadata:
 name: {{ .Values.namespaces.name }}
 labels:
 name: {{ .Values.namespaces.name }}
{{- end }}
```

####`helm-chart/templates/_helpers.tpl`
```yaml{{/* Helpers */}}
{{- define "cue.fullname" -}}
{{ printf "%s-%s" .Release.Name .Chart.Name | trunc63 | trimSuffix "-" }}
{{- end }}

{{- define "cue.labels" -}}
app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ .Chart.Name }}
app.kubernetes.io/instance: {{ .Release.Name }}
helm.sh/chart: {{ .Chart.Name }}-{{ .Chart.Version }}
{{- end }}

{{- define "cue.podAnnotations" -}}
prometheus.io/scrape: "true"
prometheus.io/port: "80"
{{- end }}
```

####`helm-chart/templates/deployment.yaml`
```yamlapiVersion: apps/v1kind: Deploymentmetadata:
 name: {{ include "cue.fullname" . }}-{{ .Values.service.name }}
 namespace: {{ .Values.namespaces.name }}
  labels: {{ include "cue.labels" . | nindent4 }}
spec:
 replicas: {{ .Values.service.replicas | default .Values.replicaCount }}
 selector:
 matchLabels:
 app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ .Values.service.name }}
 template:
 metadata:
 labels:
 app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ .Values.service.name }}
      annotations: {{ include "cue.podAnnotations" . | nindent8 }}
 spec:
 {{- if .Values.serviceAccount }}
 serviceAccountName: {{ .Values.serviceAccount }}
 {{- end }}
 containers:
 - name: {{ .Values.service.name }}
 image: "{{ .Values.image.registry }}/{{ .Values.service.name }}:{{ .Values.image.tag }}"
 imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent ports:
 - containerPort: {{ .Values.ports.http }}
 resources:
 requests: {{ .Values.resources.requests | toYaml | nindent10 }}
 limits: {{ .Values.resources.limits | toYaml | nindent10 }}
 env:
 {{- with .Values.service.env }}
 {{- toYaml . | nindent8 }}
 {{- end }}
 {{- if .Values.monitoring.fluentbit.enabled }}
 - name: fluent-bit image: fluent/fluent-bit:latest imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent resources:
 requests:{cpu: "10m", memory: "50Mi"}
 limits:{cpu: "20m", memory: "100Mi"}
 volumeMounts:
 - name: varlog mountPath: /var/log {{- end }}
 volumes:
 - name: varlog emptyDir: {}
```

####`helm-chart/templates/service.yaml`
```yamlapiVersion: v1kind: Servicemetadata:
 name: {{ .Values.service.name }}
 namespace: {{ .Values.namespaces.name }}
 labels: {{ include "cue.labels" . | nindent4 }}
spec:
 selector:
 app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ .Values.service.name }}
 ports:
 - name: http port: {{ .Values.ports.http }}
 targetPort: {{ .Values.ports.http }}
 type: ClusterIP```

####`helm-chart/templates/ingress.yaml`
```yamlapiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1kind: Ingressmetadata:
 name: {{ .Values.service.name }}-ingress
  namespace: {{ .Values.namespaces.name }}
 annotations:
 kubernetes.io/ingress.class: nginxspec:
 rules:
 - host: {{ .Values.service.name }}.example.com http:
 paths:
 - path: /
 pathType: Prefix backend:
 service:
 name: {{ .Values.service.name }}
 port: number: {{ .Values.ports.http }}
```

####`helm-chart/templates/secret.yaml`
```yamlapiVersion: v1kind: Secretmetadata:
 name: {{ .Values.service.name }}-secrets  namespace: {{ .Values.namespaces.name }}
type: Opaquedata:
 JWT_SIGNING_KEY: {{ .Values.service.jwtSigningKey | b64enc | quote }}
 # other secrets...
```

###3. Deployment Steps```bash
#1. Package the charthelm package helm-chart#2. Install the charthelm repo add local . # add local chart repohelm repo updatehelm install my-cue-platform ./cue-0.1.0.tgz \
 --namespace cue-platform \
 --create-namespace \
 --set image.tag=1.2.0 \
 --set authService.replicas=2 \
 ...

#3. Verifykubectl get all -n cue-platform```

###4. Monitoring / Logging- **Prometheus**: Pod is annotated with `prometheus.io/scrape: "true"`.
- **Fluent Bit**: Runs as a sidecar and forwards logs to external Loki/EFK stack.
- **Health‑checks**: Add `readinessProbe` and `livenessProbe` (omit for brevity).

###5. Extensibility- Each service can be listed in the `values.yaml` under a normalised key (`authService`, `bookingService`, …) where you can override `replicas`, `resources`, `env`, and any custom settings.- The `helm-chart/templates/deployment.yaml` uses these overrides to generate concise deployments.This Helm layout will let you quickly spin up the LoveAgain stack in its own namespace, provide a clean way to scale individual services, and keep the standard Kubernetes best practices for security, observability, and maintainability.

